# Comments

A single-line comment uses `//`. Anything spanning more than one line uses a `/** */` block, one `*`-prefixed line per line of text.

Write every comment in the maximum possible plain English. Its job is so tomorrow-you does not WTF — no jargon, abbreviations, or clever phrasing to decode.

```ts
// one line is fine

/**
 * More than one line goes in a block,
 * not stacked `//` lines.
 */
```
